{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "N+1 Query Analyzer & Fixer",
  "description": "Automatically analyzes PHP/Laravel code for N+1 query problems when controllers, services, or models are edited. Provides comprehensive analysis including: identification of all N+1 queries with SQL examples, optimized solutions using eager loading (with/load), select optimization, advanced techniques (withCount/withSum/subqueries), nested relationship loading, performance comparisons, missing indexes, caching strategies, pagination optimization, Laravel Debugbar output examples, automated tests for N+1 detection, and CI/CD integration setup.",
  "version": "1.0",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileEdited",
    "patterns": [
      "app/Http/Controllers/**/*.php",
      "app/Services/**/*.php",
      "app/Models/**/*.php",
      "app/Filament/Resources/**/*.php"
    ]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "N+1 QUERY ANALYSIS & OPTIMIZATION\n\nCONTEXT: Code was modified. Comprehensive N+1 query analysis and optimization.\n\nPROJECT MODELS: Building, Property, Meter, MeterReading, Invoice, InvoiceItem, Tariff, Provider, User, Tenant\n\nANALYSIS FRAMEWORK:\n\n**1. N+1 Detection:**\n- Identify problematic code patterns\n- Show generated SQL queries with examples\n- Calculate query counts for realistic datasets (10, 100, 1000 records)\n\n**2. Optimization Solutions:**\n```php\n// Eager Loading: with(), load(), lazy eager loading\n// Select Optimization: select(), addSelect()\n// Advanced: withCount(), withExists(), withSum(), subqueries\n// Nested: Deep relationships with constraints\n```\n\n**3. Performance Impact:**\n- Before/after query comparison\n- Execution time estimates\n- Memory usage considerations\n- Database-specific optimizations (SQLite)\n\n**4. Infrastructure:**\n- Missing indexes with migration code\n- Composite indexes for complex queries\n- Caching strategy and invalidation\n- Pagination optimization\n\n**5. Testing & Monitoring:**\n```php\n// Pest tests with assertQueryCount()\n// Laravel Debugbar examples\n// CI/CD integration for regression detection\n```\n\nOUTPUT:\n🔍 **Detected Issues**: N+1 patterns with SQL examples\n⚡ **Optimizations**: Complete solutions with code\n📊 **Performance Gains**: Query reduction metrics\n🧪 **Testing**: Automated N+1 detection tests\n📈 **Monitoring**: Setup for ongoing performance tracking\n\nFocus on Laravel 12 best practices and multi-tenant architecture compatibility."
  },
  "shortName": "n-plus-one-analyzer"
}